        "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events. Given that $P(A)=0.5$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.7,$ find $P(B).$",
        "worked_solution": "If $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events, then $P(A\\cap B)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, by the addition law, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B) \\\\ P(B) & =P(A\\cup B)-P(A) \\\\  & =0.7-0.5 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
